id: insult
name: Insult
type: standard
actionCost: 1
kiCost: 0
attacking: false
requiresTarget: true
special: true
usageLimit: 1/round
clashSaves: morale
insult: true
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Get under their skin. A Morale Clash, and winning leaves them Impaired and Compelled
  against you until the end of your next turn.
text: >
  Insult Maneuver [1/Round]: If physical attacks don’t work, emotional ones just might!
  –Maneuver Type: Standard Maneuver
  –Action Cost: 1 Action
  –Minions: N/A
  –KP Cost: N/A
  –Exploitable: N/A
  –Effect: Target an Opponent and make a Morale Clash against them. If you win, the
  target suffers from the Impaired Combat Condition and gains the Compelled Combat
  Condition against you until the end of your next turn.

---

# --- The Clash -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# "A Morale Clash." Morale is one of the four Saving Throws, so this is a Clash of Saving
# Throws with one named - the shape the Blockade's "Clash (Impulsive)" already has, and the
# same one the Thrust's second Clash uses with two. One named means neither side is asked
# anything: there is nothing to choose between.
#
# The first Maneuver to open one from the sheet. Every Saving Throw Clash so far has come
# out of a card - a Movement to stand in the way of, a Thrust that was already won - so
# `clashSaves` is what lets a Maneuver say it opens one when it is simply used.
#
# A tie goes to the Defender, here as everywhere else.
#
# --- What winning leaves --------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Two Combat Conditions, and only one of them is timed.
#
# "The target suffers from the Impaired Combat Condition and gains the Compelled Combat
# Condition against you until the end of your next turn." Read as: the clause at the end
# belongs to the Compelled, which is the half it also gives a subject to - "against you".
# Impaired is stated flat, and a Combat Condition with no duration stated is one that stays
# until something takes it off, which is what Condition Recovery is for.
#
# The other reading is that the clause covers both. It will carry that - it is one sentence
# with an "and" in the middle - and if that is what your table takes it to mean, the change
# is one line beside the Compelled's clock. The narrower one is built because it is the one
# that cannot quietly make the Maneuver weaker than printed: a wrongly-timed Impaired wears
# off and nobody notices, where a wrongly-permanent one gets argued about and settled.
#
# "Until the end of YOUR next turn" is the insulter's turn, so that clock is kept by them
# and the Condition sits on the target - the same split Analysis and Dirty Trick use.
#
# "Against you" is said and not tracked, which is what Compelled's own Slot has said since
# it was written: who you were told to attack is the table's to keep. The card gives them
# the sentence with the name in it.
#
# --- How it is gained ------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# A Special Maneuver, and what opens it has not been read yet. Nothing in the entry even
# names a Skill this time - the Clash is a Saving Throw - so there is not so much as a
# candidate to note down.
